1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10048,2900,279,47311,198,14085,69,2075,8,284,264,1089,87,86167,488,264,15159,77,12,16,92,87,47822,77,12,16,92,488,1124,4385,2412,488,264,62,17,87,61,17,488,264,62,16,87,488,264,62,15,14085,4648,7546,36829,11,323,1181,19703,525,12460,25780,382,22043,429,400,64,1089,28,17,3,323,400,64,62,15,28,21,21,54876,1128,374,279,3245,3204,897,315,400,91,64,15159,77,12,16,52398,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSuppose the polynomial\n$$f(x) = a_nx^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_2x^2 + a_1x + a_0$$has integer coefficients, and its roots are distinct integers.\n\nGiven that $a_n=2$ and $a_0=66$, what is the least possible value of $|a_{n-1}|$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"4309bd38936d742654b3bac0e459615edf59dc7114e6f0b1c341210ec0b92d3d"},"seconds":19.01478409767151,"seed":588933964927316561,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the polynomial \\( f(x) = 2x^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_2x^2 + a_1x + 66 \\) with integer coefficients and distinct integer roots, we can express the polynomial in its factored form as:\n\\[ f(x) = 2(x - r_1)(x - r_2) \\cdots (x - r_n) \\]\nwhere \\( r_1, r_2, \\ldots, r_n \\) are the distinct integer roots. The constant term \\( a_0 \\) is given by:\n\\[ a_0 = 2(-r_1)(-r_2) \\cdots (-r_n) = 66 \\]\nThis implies:\n\\[ 2(r_1 r_2 \\cdots r_n) = 66 \\]\nor\n\\[ r_1 r_2 \\cdots r_n = 33 \\]\nWe need to find the distinct integer roots whose product is 33. The possible sets of distinct integer factors of 33 are:\n\\[ \\{1, -1, 3, -3, 11, -11, 33, -33\\} \\]\nWe need to form a product of \\( n \\) distinct integers that equals 33. The possible factorizations are:\n\\[ 33 = 33 \\]\n\\[ 33 = 3 \\cdot 11 \\]\n\\[ 33 = (-33) \\]\n\\[ 33 = (-11) \\cdot (-3) \\]\n\\[ 33 = (-33) \\cdot 1 \\]\n\\[ 33 = 33 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 \\]\nThe only sets of distinct integers that work are \\( \\{1, 3, 11\\} \\) and \\( \\{-1, -3, -11\\} \\). We will use the set \\( \\{1, 3, 11\\} \\) for simplicity (the other set will give the same result for the sum of the roots taken one at a time).\n\nThe polynomial can be written as:\n\\[ f(x) = 2(x - 1)(x - 3)(x - 11) \\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[ f(x) = 2(x^3 - 15x^2 + 46x - 33) = 2x^3 - 30x^2 + 92x - 66 \\]\nHere, the coefficient \\( a_{n-1} = -30 \\). The absolute value is:\n\\[ |a_{n-1}| = 30 \\]\n\nWe need to check if a smaller absolute value is possible. If we use the set \\( \\{-1, -3, -11\\} \\), the polynomial is:\n\\[ f(x) = 2(x + 1)(x + 3)(x + 11) = 2(x^3 + 15x^2 + 46x + 33) = 2x^3 + 30x^2 + 92x + 66 \\]\nHere, the coefficient \\( a_{n-1} = 30 \\). The absolute value is:\n\\[ |a_{n-1}| = 30 \\]\n\nTherefore, the least possible value of \\( |a_{n-1}| \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{30} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{30}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:154"}
